@page "/settings"
@*
    The namespace deliberately does not match the folder, and must not be
    "tidied" to match it — doing so does not compile.

    This file declares a component named Settings. Under the folder-matching
    namespace Backlog.Desktop.UI.Settings it becomes
    Backlog.Desktop.UI.Settings.Settings, and that sibling namespace then shadows
    the type for everything else under Backlog.Desktop.UI. The unit tests are
    where it lands: they sit in Backlog.Desktop.UI.UnitTests, so the simple name
    Settings resolves outward to Backlog.Desktop.UI and finds the namespace
    before it ever reaches the component —

        SettingsAiUsageTests.cs(69,61): error CS0118:
            'Settings' is a namespace but is used like a type

    — for IRenderedComponent<Settings>, Render<Settings>() and the record field
    that holds it. Nothing else in the solution broke; the collision is this
    component sharing its name with the folder it moved into.

    The file still left Shell/, which was the point: Shell/ is app chrome and the
    settings screen is not. Only the published namespace stayed put, so the move
    changed no using, @@using or namespace line anywhere.

    For the same reason this folder has no _Imports.razor: the generated
    _Imports class is a type like any other, so an _Imports.razor here would
    declare Backlog.Desktop.UI.Settings and shadow the component all over again —
    and a @@namespace on it to avoid that collides with Shell/_Imports.razor
    (CS0111, one _Imports per namespace). The two lines it would have carried are
    written below instead.
*@
@namespace Backlog.Desktop.UI.Shell
@using System.Globalization
@using Backlog.Infrastructure.FileSystem
@using Backlog.Infrastructure.FileSystem.Logging
@using Backlog.Infrastructure.Claude
@using Backlog.SharedKernel
@using Backlog.SharedKernel.Results
@using Backlog.Modules.Tasks.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Tasks.Abstractions.Services
@using Backlog.Modules.Inbox.Abstractions.Services
@using Backlog.Modules.Devbook.Abstractions
@* Said in writing, which is the rule this project's _Imports.razor states for
   reaching into a context. The devbook-source control is Devbook's, and
   this screen offers the same one its pane does rather than a second copy. *@
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.Devbook
@* Sync's published surface, for the feature key the Devices tab is gated on
   and the pairing-code format the panel displays a code in. *@
@using Backlog.Modules.Sync.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Sync.Abstractions.DataTransferObjects
@using Backlog.Infrastructure.Sync
@using Backlog.Infrastructure.Sync.Sessions
@* Capture's published surface, for the Capture tab: the vocabulary of sources
   and the settings port the tab writes. *@
@using Backlog.Modules.Capture.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Capture.Abstractions.Services
@* The one namespace this page needs that the app's _Imports does not already
   carry, written here because this folder cannot have an _Imports of its own -
   see the note at the top of the file. SelectField is what the account binding
   below is drawn with. *@
@using Backlog.UI.Components.Selects
@* For the optional logger the Devices panel writes an unexpected failure to,
   rather than putting the exception's own words on screen. *@
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging
@inject WorkspaceSettingsStore Store
@* Injected rather than read off IServiceProvider the way the sync collaborators
   below are: those are optional and feature-gated, and this is neither. A host
   that has not registered it should fail loudly at startup rather than quietly
   drop the section that edits it. *@
@inject IWorkingHoursSettings WorkingWeek
@inject GitHubIntegration GitHub
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IAppFeatureSettings Features
@inject AzureFoundrySettingsStore AzureFoundry
@inject ILocalGitRepositoryService LocalGit
@inject ClaudeSettingsStore Claude
@inject IDevbookFolderSource DevbookFolders
@inject DevbookSourceSelection DevbookSource
@* The two sync collaborators are read off this rather than injected; see the
   Devices section of the code block for why. *@
@inject IServiceProvider Services
@implements IDisposable

@*
    The one screen in this app with a form control, and it earns it: a folder
    path is not something you can type inline into a backlog entry. It still
    follows the house rule - no save button. Committing the field (blur or
    Enter) moves the store.
*@

<div class="shell shell--settings">
    <header class="app-header">
        @* The title and the way back, and nothing else. The Report issue button
           was here because a per-page mount was the only kind there was, and this
           page needing one of its own is exactly the duplication the app-shell
           footer removes: MainLayout mounts it once, below this page too. *@
        <h1>Settings</h1>
        <a class="icon-link" href="" data-testid="back-link" title="Back to your tasks" aria-label="Back to your tasks">←</a>
    </header>

    @* The pill strip is the shared Tabs component wearing this page's classes.
       Arrow-key movement between the pills comes with it. *@
    <Tabs Bare="true"
          ListElement="nav"
          ListCssClass="settings-tabs"
          AriaLabel="Settings pages"
          TabCssClass="settings-tab"
          ActiveTabCssClass="settings-tab settings-tab--active"
          ActiveId="@ActivePageId"
          ActiveIdChanged="ShowSettingsPageById">

        <TabPanel Id="features" Title="Features" Element="section" BaseClass="setting" aria-label="Feature settings">
            <h2 class="setting__title">Features</h2>
            <p class="setting__description">
                Turn off parts of the app that are not ready yet. Tasks stays available.
            </p>
            @* Two headings rather than one grid of thirteen. A reader turning
               something off is asking one of two quite different questions —
               "do I want this area of the product" or "do I want this thing the
               whole product uses" — and the flat list answered neither. *@
            @foreach (var section in AppFeatures.Sections)
            {
            <h3 class="feature-group__title">@section.Title</h3>
            <p class="feature-group__description">@section.Description</p>
            <div class="feature-flags" role="list" aria-label="@($"{section.Title} feature flags")">
                @foreach (var feature in section.Features)
                {
                    @* A flag row is the shared Toggle in its native-checkbox
                       shape: the whole row is a label, so the box is reachable
                       by clicking the text. *@
                    <Toggle NativeCheckbox="true"
                            BaseClass="feature-flag"
                            CssClass="@(feature.AlwaysEnabled ? "feature-flag--locked" : null)"
                            TextCssClass="feature-flag__content"
                            LabelCssClass="feature-flag__title"
                            DescriptionCssClass="feature-flag__description"
                            Label="@feature.Name"
                            Description="@feature.Description"
                            Checked="@Features.IsEnabled(feature.Key)"
                            CheckedChanged="enabled => SetFeatureEnabled(feature, enabled)"
                            Disabled="@feature.AlwaysEnabled"
                            role="listitem">
                        @* The maturity flag qualifies the name of the thing, so it
                           goes on the label's line rather than into the note below
                           it: somebody scanning the switches has to see which ones
                           are unfinished without reading a paragraph each. It
                           renders nothing for a released feature, which is why
                           there is no @@if around it.

                           Unconditional on the switch, unlike everywhere else this
                           badge appears — this row *is* the switch, so it describes
                           the feature whether or not it is currently on. *@
                        <LabelSuffix>
                            <FeatureStatusBadge Status="@AppFeatureStatusBadge.Slug(feature.Status)"
                                                Title="@AppFeatureStatusBadge.Title(feature.Status)"
                                                TestId="@($"feature-status-{feature.Key}")" />
                        </LabelSuffix>
                        <TextContent>
                            @if (feature.AlwaysEnabled)
                            {
                                <span class="feature-flag__status">Always available</span>
                            }
                        </TextContent>
                    </Toggle>

                    @if (IsUsageMetricsFeature(feature) && UsageMetricsEnabled)
                    {
                        <p class="setting__note" data-testid="usage-api-endpoints-context-note">
                            Configure organization usage API endpoints on the AI tab.
                        </p>
                    }
                }
            </div>
            }
            @* The library's alert wearing this page's note class. It renders
               nothing when the message is empty, which is what the @@if around the
               hand-rolled paragraph used to do. *@
            <Alert Message="@_featureMessage" BaseClass="setting__note" Role="status" />
        </TabPanel>

    @if (IsSettingsPageAvailable(SettingsPage.Ai))
    {
        <TabPanel Id="ai" Title="AI" Element="section" BaseClass="setting" aria-label="AI settings">
            @* Two cards that configure unrelated things, so on a window with
               the room they stand side by side rather than one under the other. *@
            <div class="setting-columns">
                @if (UsageMetricsEnabled)
                {
                    @* Claude and GitHub are two vendors, two credentials and two failure
                       modes, so they are two cards. One card mixing them meant a change to
                       either endpoint saved both and reported through a single status line
                       that could not say which vendor it was talking about. *@
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="claude-usage-settings" aria-label="Claude usage API settings">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Claude usage API</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            What Backlog needs to read your Claude usage and cost reports. One card per
                            organization you belong to - a personal Console beside an employer's - and
                            the dashboard adds their spend up.
                        </p>

                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="claude-accounts-status" role="status">
                            <span>@ClaudeAccountsSummary()</span>
                        </p>

                        @* One subpage per account, the same shared strip the GitHub account
                           cards use - only what is inside the card differs. There is always
                           at least one: the store keeps a blank account rather than an empty
                           list, so a fresh install sees the fields straight away. *@
                        <Tabs Bare="true"
                              ListCssClass="repo-subpages"
                              ListTestId="claude-account-subpages"
                              AriaLabel="Claude account pages"
                              TabCssClass="repo-subpage"
                              ActiveTabCssClass="repo-subpage repo-subpage--active"
                              ActiveId="@ActiveClaudeAccount.Id"
                              ActiveIdChanged="ShowClaudeAccountPage">
                            @foreach (var account in Claude.Current.Accounts)
                            {
                                var claudeAccount = account;

                                @* A plain Title rather than TitleContent: the label changes as
                                   the card is filled in, and a string title is what the strip
                                   knows how to notice changing. *@
                                <TabPanel Id="@claudeAccount.Id"
                                          Title="@claudeAccount.Label"
                                          TabTestId="claude-account-subpage-tab"
                                          Element="article"
                                          BaseClass="repo-card"
                                          TestId="claude-account-card"
                                          aria-label="@($"{claudeAccount.Label} Claude account settings")">
                                    <ChildContent>
                                        <header class="repo-card__header">
                                            <div>
                                                <h3 class="repo-card__title">@claudeAccount.Label</h3>
                                                <p class="repo-card__meta">
                                                    <code>@claudeAccount.ApiEndpoint</code>
                                                </p>
                                            </div>

                                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                       TestId="remove-claude-account-button"
                                                       OnClick="() => RemoveClaudeAccount(claudeAccount)">
                                                Forget this account
                                            </AppButton>
                                        </header>

                                        @* Every field on this page is the shared TextField wearing
                                           the page's own label and input classes. Bare, because a
                                           settings section lays its label and box out itself, and a
                                           grid wrapper between them would move the spacing. *@
                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Name (optional)"
                                                   Id="@($"claude-account-name-{claudeAccount.Id}")"
                                                   data-testid="claude-account-name-input"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   Placeholder="personal, work..."
                                                   HelpText="Only for telling two accounts apart on this page."
                                                   Value="@Draft(_draftClaudeNames, claudeAccount)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftClaudeNames[claudeAccount.Id] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyClaudeUsageSettings(claudeAccount)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnClaudeUsageKeyDown(e, claudeAccount)" />

                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Organization API endpoint"
                                                   Id="@($"claude-usage-endpoint-{claudeAccount.Id}")"
                                                   data-testid="claude-usage-endpoint-input"
                                                   Type="url"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   Value="@Draft(_draftClaudeEndpoints, claudeAccount)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftClaudeEndpoints[claudeAccount.Id] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyClaudeUsageSettings(claudeAccount)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnClaudeUsageKeyDown(e, claudeAccount)" />

                                        @* Which actor in this Claude organization is you. Not an endpoint
                                           and not a secret, but it belongs beside them rather than in a
                                           section of its own: it is the third thing needed before an
                                           organization-scoped usage report can be read as a personal one.
                                           The Claude Code report lists every actor in the organization, and
                                           there is no endpoint that says which one an admin key belongs to
                                           - an admin key belongs to the organization, not to a person. *@
                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Your Claude account"
                                                   Id="@($"claude-usage-actor-{claudeAccount.Id}")"
                                                   data-testid="claude-usage-actor-input"
                                                   Type="email"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   Value="@Draft(_draftClaudeActors, claudeAccount)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftClaudeActors[claudeAccount.Id] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyClaudeUsageSettings(claudeAccount)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnClaudeUsageKeyDown(e, claudeAccount)" />

                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Claude API key"
                                                   Id="@($"claude-api-key-{claudeAccount.Id}")"
                                                   data-testid="claude-api-key-input"
                                                   Type="password"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   HelpText="@ClaudeApiKeyHint(claudeAccount)"
                                                   Placeholder="@(claudeAccount.AdminApiKey is null ? "sk-ant-admin01-..." : "stored - hidden")"
                                                   Value="@Draft(_draftClaudeApiKeys, claudeAccount)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftClaudeApiKeys[claudeAccount.Id] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyClaudeApiKey(claudeAccount)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnClaudeApiKeyDown(e, claudeAccount)" />

                                        @* The workspace narrows the message and cost reports. It does not
                                           narrow the Claude Code report, which is per-actor - that is what
                                           the account field above is for. *@
                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Workspace (optional)"
                                                   Id="@($"claude-workspace-{claudeAccount.Id}")"
                                                   data-testid="claude-workspace-input"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   Placeholder="wrkspc_..."
                                                   HelpText="Reports one workspace instead of the whole organization. Leave it empty for everything."
                                                   Value="@Draft(_draftClaudeWorkspaces, claudeAccount)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftClaudeWorkspaces[claudeAccount.Id] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyClaudeUsageSettings(claudeAccount)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnClaudeUsageKeyDown(e, claudeAccount)" />

                                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="claude-usage-status" role="status">
                                            @if (_claudeAccountMessages.GetValueOrDefault(claudeAccount.Id) is { } claudeMessage)
                                            {
                                                <span>@claudeMessage</span>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span>
                                                    Usage metrics calls Claude at <code>@claudeAccount.ApiEndpoint</code>.
                                                    @if (!claudeAccount.IsConfigured)
                                                    {
                                                        <text> Claude needs a key before it can report anything.</text>
                                                    }
                                                    @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(claudeAccount.Actor))
                                                    {
                                                        <text> The dashboard needs your Claude account before it can show your spend rather than the whole organization's.</text>
                                                    }
                                                    else
                                                    {
                                                        <text> The dashboard reports Claude usage for <code>@claudeAccount.Actor</code>.</text>
                                                    }
                                                </span>
                                            }
                                        </p>

                                        <div class="setting__actions">
                                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                       data-testid="claude-clear-key-button"
                                                       Disabled="@(claudeAccount.AdminApiKey is null)"
                                                       OnClick="() => ClearClaudeApiKey(claudeAccount)">
                                                Forget Claude key
                                            </AppButton>
                                        </div>
                                    </ChildContent>
                                </TabPanel>
                            }
                        </Tabs>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                       TestId="add-claude-account-button"
                                       OnClick="AddClaudeAccount">
                                Add another Claude account
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        <p class="setting__note">
                            Everything here is auto-saved. The keys are kept in <code>@Claude.SettingsPath</code> - outside the backlog folder, so they are never synced or committed with entries.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="setting" data-testid="github-usage-settings" aria-label="GitHub usage API settings">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">GitHub usage API</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            What Backlog needs to read organization Copilot seat activity.
                        </p>

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="Organization API endpoint"
                                   Id="github-usage-endpoint"
                                   data-testid="github-usage-endpoint-input"
                                   Type="url"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Value="@_draftGitHubUsageEndpoint"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftGitHubUsageEndpoint = value"
                                   @onchange="ApplyGitHubUsageSettings"
                                   @onkeydown="OnGitHubUsageKeyDown" />

                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="github-usage-status" role="status">
                            @if (_gitHubUsageMessage is not null)
                            {
                                <span>@_gitHubUsageMessage</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>Usage metrics calls GitHub at <code>@GitHub.Settings.Current.ApiEndpoint</code> as whichever account this machine is signed in as. Copilot metrics are organization-scoped and owner-only.</span>
                            }
                        </p>

                        @* Every configured account is read as well, each at its own endpoint
                           - a login on an Enterprise Server is a login on a different API.
                           Listed here so the whole picture is on one card; edited on the
                           account's own card, because the endpoint is a fact about the
                           account rather than about usage reporting. *@
                        @foreach (var account in ConfiguredAccounts)
                        {
                            <p class="setting__status" data-testid="github-usage-account-endpoint" role="status">
                                <span>
                                    Usage for <code>@account.Login</code> is read at
                                    <code>@(account.ApiEndpoint ?? GitHub.Settings.Current.ApiEndpoint)</code>@(account.ApiEndpoint is null ? " - the endpoint above." : ".")
                                </span>
                            </p>
                        }

                        @* No token field here. GitHub authenticates per account, on the
                           Accounts tab, and signing in with the GitHub CLI is preferred
                           over a token at all - so a second place to type one would be a
                           second place for it to go stale. *@
                        <p class="setting__note">
                            Auto-saved. GitHub access and a per-account endpoint are set up on the Accounts tab, or by signing in with the GitHub CLI.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                }

                @if (AiAssistantEnabled)
                {
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="azure-foundry-settings" aria-label="Azure Foundry AI settings">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Azure Foundry AI</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Connect Backlog to an Azure Foundry chat deployment. The app sends the
                            visible backlog content and your question to that deployment only when
                            you ask.
                        </p>

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="Endpoint"
                                   Id="azure-foundry-endpoint"
                                   data-testid="azure-foundry-endpoint-input"
                                   Type="url"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Placeholder="https://your-resource.openai.azure.com"
                                   Value="@_draftAzureFoundryEndpoint"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftAzureFoundryEndpoint = value"
                                   @onchange="ApplyAzureFoundryConnection"
                                   @onkeydown="OnAzureFoundryKeyDown" />

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="Deployment"
                                   Id="azure-foundry-deployment"
                                   data-testid="azure-foundry-deployment-input"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Placeholder="gpt-5.4"
                                   Value="@_draftAzureFoundryDeployment"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftAzureFoundryDeployment = value"
                                   @onchange="ApplyAzureFoundryConnection"
                                   @onkeydown="OnAzureFoundryKeyDown" />

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="API version"
                                   Id="azure-foundry-api-version"
                                   data-testid="azure-foundry-api-version-input"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Value="@_draftAzureFoundryApiVersion"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftAzureFoundryApiVersion = value"
                                   @onchange="ApplyAzureFoundryConnection"
                                   @onkeydown="OnAzureFoundryKeyDown" />

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="API key"
                                   Id="azure-foundry-api-key"
                                   data-testid="azure-foundry-api-key-input"
                                   Type="password"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Placeholder="@(AzureFoundry.Current.ApiKey is null ? "key" : "stored - hidden")"
                                   Value="@_draftAzureFoundryApiKey"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftAzureFoundryApiKey = value"
                                   @onchange="ApplyAzureFoundryApiKey"
                                   @onkeydown="OnAzureFoundryApiKeyDown" />

                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="azure-foundry-status" role="status">
                            @if (_azureFoundryMessage is not null)
                            {
                                <span>@_azureFoundryMessage</span>
                            }
                            else if (AzureFoundry.Current.IsConfigured)
                            {
                                <span>AI is connected to <code>@AzureFoundry.Current.Deployment</code>.</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>AI needs an endpoint, deployment, and API key before it can answer questions.</span>
                            }
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                       data-testid="azure-foundry-clear-key-button"
                                       Disabled="@(AzureFoundry.Current.ApiKey is null)"
                                       OnClick="ClearAzureFoundryApiKey">
                                Forget API key
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        <p class="setting__note">
                            The key is kept in <code>@AzureFoundry.SettingsPath</code> - outside the backlog folder, so it is never synced or committed with entries.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                }
            </div>
        </TabPanel>
    }

        <TabPanel Id="storage" Title="Storage" Element="section" BaseClass="setting" aria-label="Storage settings">
            @* Three blocks that each carry their own heading, so the columns
               read as three settings rather than as one cut into pieces: where
               the backlog is, where it is backed up to, and the working week.
               The devbook cache sits under the first because it follows the
               folder by default. *@
            <div class="setting-columns">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="setting__title">Where the backlog is stored</h2>
                    @* This paragraph used to say every entry was its own markdown file
                       and to suggest pointing the folder at a synced one. Both halves
                       stopped being true when the store became one database, and the
                       suggestion cost somebody their edits - see R9 in
                       .arc42/11-risks-and-technical-debt.md. The warning is the copy
                       now, and SettingsStorageCopyTests pins it. *@
                    <p class="setting__body" data-testid="storage-path-description">
                        The whole backlog is one SQLite database in this folder. Your text stays
                        markdown inside it, but it is a single binary file - so keep this on a local
                        disk. A file-sync folder like OneDrive or Dropbox cannot merge it, and two
                        machines writing it will lose edits.
                    </p>

                    @* The concrete half of the paragraph above. That one can say
                       what a synced folder does to the database; only this can say
                       that the folder in the field is one - which is the gap local
                       ADR 0005 left the copy holding, because a root that followed
                       the retired advice stays where it is. It names the provider
                       and stops there: the root is the reader's choice and this
                       warns rather than prevents. Renders nothing when the store
                       recognised nothing, which is also what an unknown machine
                       and an unreadable disk produce. *@
                    <Alert Message="@SyncedRootWarning"
                           BaseClass="setting__warning"
                           Id="storage-path-sync-warning"
                           TestId="storage-path-sync-warning" />

                    @* The error class goes on InputCssClass, not ErrorMessage: this
                       page reports the reason in its own status paragraph below, and
                       ErrorMessage would render a second one as an Alert.

                       No @onchange, and deliberately. The field used to commit a move
                       on change, which fires on blur - so clicking "Switch without
                       moving" after typing a folder moved the backlog there first and
                       then switched to it, and the button could never do what it said.
                       Enter still moves, because a key pressed on purpose is a choice;
                       leaving the field is not. *@
                    <TextField Bare="true"
                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                               InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_error)"
                               Label="Folder"
                               Id="storage-path"
                               data-testid="storage-path-input"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               autocomplete="off"
                               aria-describedby="@StoragePathDescribedBy"
                               Value="@_draftPath"
                               ValueChanged="value => _draftPath = value"
                               @onkeydown="OnKeyDownAsync" />

                    <p class="setting__status" id="storage-path-status" data-testid="storage-path-status" role="status">
                        @if (_error is not null)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--error">@_error</span>
                        }
                        else if (_moved && _copied)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--ok">Moved. The backlog was copied here and now loads from this folder; the copy in <code>@_previousRoot</code> was left as it was.</span>
                        }
                        else if (_moved)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--ok">Switched. Entries now load from this folder - nothing was copied.</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>Tasks live in <code>@Store.DatabasePath</code>@(Store.IsDefaultRoot ? " - the default location." : ".") Inbox is prepared at <code>@Store.InboxDirectory</code>.</span>
                        }
                    </p>

                    @* Two ways to leave a folder, each a button, plus the default
                       folder as the move it most often is. Moving takes the backlog
                       along; switching leaves it behind and reads whatever the other
                       folder holds. Switching used to be the only way, which is how
                       "Use the default folder" came to empty a backlog whose database
                       was still sitting on OneDrive - and moving used to be only the
                       default button and the field's own change event, so the folder
                       somebody typed had no button that said "move" over it. *@
                    <div class="setting__actions">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   data-testid="move-storage-path"
                                   Disabled="@IsCurrentRootDraft"
                                   OnClick="ApplyAsync">
                            Move to this folder
                        </AppButton>
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   data-testid="switch-storage-path"
                                   Disabled="@IsCurrentRootDraft"
                                   OnClick="SwitchAsync">
                            Switch without moving
                        </AppButton>
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   data-testid="reset-storage-path"
                                   Disabled="@Store.IsDefaultRoot"
                                   OnClick="MoveToDefaultAsync">
                            Move to the default folder
                        </AppButton>
                    </div>

                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Moving takes the backlog along: the database, the inbox folder and the
                        app's own configuration are copied there, and the app reads from the
                        new folder from then on. Anything else you keep in the folder stays where
                        it is, and so does the old copy - delete it yourself once you are sure. A
                        folder that already holds a backlog is never written over. Switch without
                        moving to open a backlog that already lives in the folder you entered; that
                        copies nothing.
                    </p>


                @* Under the storage folder by default, so a backlog moved to
                   another disk takes the default location of what was fetched
                   to read beside it along. It is a setting rather than a
                   constant because a machine with a small system drive and a
                   large one for work is an ordinary machine. Not backed up and
                   not moved: a snapshot is a disposable copy of a commit that
                   can always be fetched again. *@
                <div class="devbook-folders" data-testid="devbook-cache-settings">
                    <h3 class="devbook-folders__title">Branch snapshot folder</h3>
                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Where the devbook fetched from a repository branch is cached. It sits under the
                        storage folder unless you point it elsewhere; clear the field to return it there.
                        Changing this leaves the old folder alone; the new one refills on the next fetch.
                    </p>
                    <TextField Bare="true"
                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                               InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_devbookCacheError)"
                               Label="Snapshot folder"
                               Id="devbook-cache-directory"
                               data-testid="devbook-cache-directory-input"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               autocomplete="off"
                               Placeholder="@Store.DefaultDevbookCacheDirectory"
                               aria-describedby="devbook-cache-status"
                               Value="@_draftDevbookCacheDirectory"
                               ValueChanged="value => _draftDevbookCacheDirectory = value"
                               @onchange="ApplyDevbookCacheDirectory"
                               @onkeydown="OnDevbookCacheDirectoryKeyDown" />
                    <p class="setting__status" id="devbook-cache-status" data-testid="devbook-cache-status" role="status">
                        @if (_devbookCacheError is not null)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--error">@_devbookCacheError</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>Snapshots: <code>@Store.DevbookCacheDirectory</code>@(Store.IsDefaultDevbookCacheDirectory ? " - under the storage folder." : ".")</span>
                        }
                    </p>
                </div>
                </div>

                @* One-way, and the copy says so twice: a backup is a copy that
                   leaves, and nothing here ever reads the repository back into
                   the folder. A backup that came home on its own would be file
                   sync by another name, and R9 in .arc42/11-risks-and-technical-debt.md
                   is what that did to this database. Local ADR 0010 is the
                   decision; BackupWorker is the mechanism. *@
                <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="storage-backup-settings">
                    <h2 class="setting__title">Backup</h2>
                    <p class="setting__body">
                        A copy of the database is committed to a GitHub repository you name - on a
                        schedule, or when you press the button. Each backup replaces the last one at
                        <code>@BackupWorker.RepositoryPath</code> and the repository's history keeps the
                        rest; a database that has not changed makes no commit. Nothing comes back on
                        its own: restoring a backup is putting the file back by hand.
                    </p>

                    <TextField Bare="true"
                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                               InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_storageRepositoryError)"
                               Label="Repository"
                               Id="storage-repository"
                               data-testid="storage-repository-input"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               autocomplete="off"
                               Placeholder="owner/repo"
                               aria-describedby="storage-repository-status"
                               Value="@_draftStorageRepository"
                               ValueChanged="value => _draftStorageRepository = value"
                               @onchange="ApplyStorageRepository"
                               @onkeydown="OnStorageRepositoryKeyDown" />

                    <p class="setting__status" id="storage-repository-status" data-testid="storage-repository-status" role="status">
                        @if (_storageRepositoryError is not null)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--error">@_storageRepositoryError</span>
                        }
                        else if (Store.RootRepository is { } storageRepository)
                        {
                            <span>Backs up to <code>@storageRepository.FullName</code>, using the GitHub account this machine is signed in with.</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>No backup repository configured.</span>
                        }
                    </p>

                    @* A cadence picked from three, which is the shape SelectField
                       exists for; the day and the time are shown only when the
                       cadence gives them something to decide. Form-shaped, the way
                       the account credential select is, because a bare caption
                       beside bordered inputs does not read as a control. *@
                    <SelectField Form="true"
                                 Label="Schedule"
                                 Id="storage-backup-cadence"
                                 TestId="storage-backup-cadence"
                                 LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                 SelectCssClass="setting__input"
                                 CurrentValue="@Store.BackupSchedule.Cadence.ToString()"
                                 Options="@BackupCadenceOptions"
                                 OnChanged="ApplyBackupCadence" />

                    @if (Store.BackupSchedule.Cadence is BackupCadence.Weekly)
                    {
                        <SelectField Form="true"
                                     Label="On"
                                     Id="storage-backup-day"
                                     TestId="storage-backup-day"
                                     LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                     SelectCssClass="setting__input"
                                     CurrentValue="@Store.BackupSchedule.Day.ToString()"
                                     Options="@BackupDayOptions"
                                     OnChanged="ApplyBackupDay" />
                    }

                    @if (Store.BackupSchedule.IsScheduled)
                    {
                        @* Committed from the change event's own value rather than
                           through ValueChanged, for the reason the working-week
                           rows give: a time input raises empty input events while
                           a time is half typed. *@
                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_backupScheduleError)"
                                   Label="At"
                                   Id="storage-backup-time"
                                   data-testid="storage-backup-time"
                                   Type="time"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   aria-describedby="storage-backup-status"
                                   Value="@BackupTimeDraft"
                                   @onchange="ApplyBackupTime"
                                   @onkeydown="OnBackupTimeKeyDown" />
                    }

                    <p class="setting__status @(BackupStatusIsFailure ? "setting__status--error" : null)"
                       id="storage-backup-status"
                       data-testid="storage-backup-status"
                       role="@(BackupStatusIsFailure ? "alert" : "status")">
                        <span>@BackupStatusLine</span>
                    </p>

                    <div class="setting__actions">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   TestId="storage-backup-now"
                                   Busy="@(_backup?.IsRunning ?? false)"
                                   Disabled="@(_backup is null || Store.RootRepository is null)"
                                   OnClick="BackUpNow">
                            Back up now
                        </AppButton>
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   data-testid="clear-storage-repository-button"
                                   Disabled="@(Store.RootRepository is null)"
                                   OnClick="ClearStorageRepository">
                            Clear backup repository
                        </AppButton>
                    </div>

                    @if (_backup is not null)
                    {
                        <p class="setting__note">
                            What the last backup did is kept in <code>@_backup.StorePath</code>, beside the
                            app's other per-user files rather than in the backlog folder.
                        </p>
                    }
                </div>

                @* Not a storage setting, and it is here because this is the only
                   tab that is always on screen and already carries a preference
                   rather than a credential or a flag — the backup schedule beside
                   it is one too. The AI tab would have read better next to the
                   surface that uses this, but it disappears behind two feature
                   flags, and a working week nobody can reach is worse than one
                   filed under the wrong heading. *@
                <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="working-hours-settings">
                    <h3 class="devbook-folders__title">Your working week</h3>
                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Which hours you mean to be working. This changes no figure - work is counted
                        the same whenever it happened - it only lets the dashboard shade the hours
                        you meant to be at work, so out-of-hours work is something you can see rather
                        than something you have to work out. Each day stands on its own, and a day
                        you turn off keeps its hours for when you turn it back on.
                    </p>

                    <div class="working-week">
                        @foreach (var day in WorkingHours.Week)
                        {
                            var working = WorkingWeek.Current.On(day);
                            var slug = day.ToString().ToLowerInvariant();

                            <div class="working-day" data-testid="working-hours-row">
                                @* Checkbox rather than Toggle, the way the knowledge
                                   rows above do it: the box leads the row and the day
                                   name is what it is clicked by. *@
                                <Checkbox CssClass="devbook-folder__toggle"
                                          Label="@day.ToString()"
                                          Checked="@working.Working"
                                          CheckedChanged="value => SetWorkingDayEnabled(day, value)"
                                          data-testid="@($"working-hours-{slug}-enabled")" />

                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                           InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                           AriaLabel="@($"{day} start")"
                                           Id="@($"working-hours-{slug}-start")"
                                           data-testid="@($"working-hours-{slug}-start")"
                                           Type="time"
                                           autocomplete="off"
                                           aria-describedby="working-hours-status"
                                           Disabled="@(!working.Working)"
                                           Value="@WorkingHoursDraft(day, start: true)"
                                           @onchange="e => ApplyWorkingTime(day, start: true, e)"
                                           @onkeydown="e => OnWorkingHoursKeyDown(e, day, start: true)" />

                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                           InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                           AriaLabel="@($"{day} end")"
                                           Id="@($"working-hours-{slug}-end")"
                                           data-testid="@($"working-hours-{slug}-end")"
                                           Type="time"
                                           autocomplete="off"
                                           aria-describedby="working-hours-status"
                                           Disabled="@(!working.Working)"
                                           Value="@WorkingHoursDraft(day, start: false)"
                                           @onchange="e => ApplyWorkingTime(day, start: false, e)"
                                           @onkeydown="e => OnWorkingHoursKeyDown(e, day, start: false)" />
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <p class="setting__status" id="working-hours-status" data-testid="working-hours-status" role="status">
                        @if (_workingHoursError is not null)
                        {
                            <span class="setting__status--error">@_workingHoursError</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>@WorkingWeekSummary()</span>
                        }
                    </p>

                    <div class="setting__actions">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   data-testid="working-hours-reset-button"
                                   Disabled="@IsDefaultWorkingWeek"
                                   OnClick="ResetWorkingHours">
                            Back to Monday to Friday
                        </AppButton>
                    </div>

                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Kept in <code>@WorkingWeek.SettingsPath</code>, beside the app's other
                        per-user choices rather than in the backlog folder - it is yours, not the
                        workspace's.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </TabPanel>

    @if (IsSettingsPageAvailable(SettingsPage.Accounts))
    {
        @* Read before Repositories on purpose: a repository is bound to one of
           these, so the list it is picked from has to be the thing already in
           front of somebody by the time they get there. *@
        <TabPanel Id="accounts"
                  Title="Accounts"
                  Element="section"
                  BaseClass="setting"
                  TestId="github-accounts-settings"
                  aria-label="Account settings">
            <h2 class="setting__title">GitHub accounts</h2>
            <p class="setting__body">
                The GitHub identities this machine can speak as. A repository is worked as one of
                them on the Repositories tab, so a call for one owner's repository never leaves
                carrying another owner's identity.
            </p>

            <p class="setting__status" data-testid="github-accounts-status" role="status">
                @if (_accountMessage is not null)
                {
                    <span class="setting__status--error">@_accountMessage</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span>@AccountsSummary()</span>
                }
            </p>

            @* A binding this machine cannot meet is a real state with a name, not
               a fault: it is the ordinary day-one shape of a second install. It is
               said here as well as on the repository's own card, because this panel
               is the place somebody comes to fix it. *@
            @foreach (var unsatisfied in UnsatisfiedBindings())
            {
                <p class="setting__status" data-testid="unsatisfied-binding" role="status">
                    <span class="setting__status--error">@unsatisfied</span>
                </p>
            }

            <div class="setting-columns">
                <div data-testid="gh-cli-accounts">
                    <h3 class="devbook-folders__title">Signed in with the GitHub CLI</h3>
                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Adding one of these is the route that holds no secret: Backlog asks
                        <code>gh</code> for a token when a call needs one and never writes it down,
                        so the CLI keeps refreshing and revoking it.
                    </p>

                    @if (DiscoverableCliAccounts.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="setting__note" data-testid="gh-cli-accounts-empty">
                            @(_cliAccounts.Count == 0
                                ? "The GitHub CLI reported no accounts on this machine. Add a login opposite and paste a personal access token for it instead."
                                : "Every account the GitHub CLI is signed in to is already configured.")
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            @foreach (var discovered in DiscoverableCliAccounts)
                            {
                                var candidate = discovered;

                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                           TestId="add-gh-cli-account-button"
                                           OnClick="() => AddCliAccount(candidate)">
                                    Add @candidate.Login
                                </AppButton>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    <div class="setting__actions">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   TestId="gh-cli-accounts-refresh-button"
                                   OnClick="RefreshCliAccountsAsync">
                            Look again
                        </AppButton>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div data-testid="add-account">
                    <h3 class="devbook-folders__title">Add an account by login</h3>
                    <p class="setting__note">
                        For a machine without the GitHub CLI, or a login it does not know about.
                        Leaving the field saves it, the way every other box on this page works.
                        Give it a personal access token on its own card below.
                    </p>

                    <TextField Bare="true"
                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                               InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_accountMessage)"
                               Label="GitHub login"
                               Id="account-login"
                               data-testid="add-account-login-input"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               autocomplete="off"
                               aria-describedby="github-accounts-status"
                               Placeholder="octocat"
                               Value="@_draftAccountLogin"
                               ValueChanged="value => _draftAccountLogin = value"
                               @onchange="AddAccountFromDraft"
                               @onkeydown="OnAccountLoginKeyDown" />

                    <div class="setting__actions">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   TestId="add-account-button"
                                   OnClick="AddAccountFromDraft">
                            Add account
                        </AppButton>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            @if (ConfiguredAccounts.Count > 0)
            {
                @* One subpage per account, the same shared strip the repository
                   cards below use - only what is inside the card differs. *@
                <Tabs Bare="true"
                      ListCssClass="repo-subpages"
                      ListTestId="account-subpages"
                      AriaLabel="Account pages"
                      TabCssClass="repo-subpage"
                      ActiveTabCssClass="repo-subpage repo-subpage--active"
                      ActiveId="@ActiveAccount?.Login"
                      ActiveIdChanged="ShowAccountPage">
                    @foreach (var account in ConfiguredAccounts)
                    {
                        var activeAccount = account;

                        <TabPanel Id="@activeAccount.Login"
                                  TabTestId="account-subpage-tab"
                                  Element="article"
                                  BaseClass="repo-card"
                                  TestId="github-account-card"
                                  aria-label="@($"{activeAccount.Login} account settings")">
                            <TitleContent>
                                <span>@activeAccount.Label</span>
                            </TitleContent>
                            <ChildContent>
                                <header class="repo-card__header">
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 class="repo-card__title">@activeAccount.Login</h3>
                                        <p class="repo-card__meta">
                                            <code>@(activeAccount.Host ?? "github.com")</code>
                                        </p>
                                    </div>

                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               TestId="remove-account-button"
                                               OnClick="() => RemoveAccount(activeAccount)">
                                        Forget this account
                                    </AppButton>
                                </header>

                                @* A name picked from a list of two, which is the shape
                                   SelectField exists for. Not the colour swatches'
                                   radiogroup: those are a radiogroup because a colour
                                   has to be seen to be chosen, and a credential kind is
                                   a word. *@
                                <SelectField Form="true"
                                             Label="Credential"
                                             Id="@($"account-credential-{activeAccount.Login}")"
                                             TestId="account-credential-select"
                                             LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                             SelectCssClass="setting__input"
                                             CurrentValue="@activeAccount.Credential.ToString()"
                                             Options="@CredentialKindOptions"
                                             HelpText="How this machine gets a token for this login when a call needs one."
                                             OnChanged="kind => ApplyAccountCredential(activeAccount, kind)" />

                                @if (activeAccount.Credential is GitHubCredentialKind.PersonalAccessToken)
                                {
                                    <TextField Bare="true"
                                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                               InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                               Label="Personal access token"
                                               Id="@($"account-token-{activeAccount.Login}")"
                                               data-testid="account-token-input"
                                               type="password"
                                               spellcheck="false"
                                               autocomplete="off"
                                               Placeholder="@(activeAccount.HasToken ? "stored - hidden" : "ghp_...")"
                                               Value="@AccountTokenDraft(activeAccount)"
                                               ValueChanged="value => _draftAccountTokens[activeAccount.Login] = value"
                                               @onchange="() => ApplyAccountToken(activeAccount)"
                                               @onkeydown="e => OnAccountTokenKeyDown(e, activeAccount)" />

                                    <div class="setting__actions">
                                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                   TestId="account-clear-token-button"
                                                   Disabled="@(!activeAccount.HasToken)"
                                                   OnClick="() => ClearAccountToken(activeAccount)">
                                            Forget this token
                                        </AppButton>
                                    </div>
                                }

                                @* Where this login's API is. Blank follows the install-wide
                                   endpoint on the AI tab, which is every github.com account;
                                   a GitHub Enterprise Server login names its own here. *@
                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                           LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                           InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                           Label="API endpoint (optional)"
                                           Id="@($"account-endpoint-{activeAccount.Login}")"
                                           data-testid="account-endpoint-input"
                                           Type="url"
                                           spellcheck="false"
                                           autocomplete="off"
                                           Placeholder="@GitHub.Settings.Current.ApiEndpoint"
                                           HelpText="Leave it empty to use the install-wide endpoint. Set it for a login on a GitHub Enterprise Server."
                                           Value="@AccountEndpointDraft(activeAccount)"
                                           ValueChanged="value => _draftAccountEndpoints[activeAccount.Login] = value"
                                           @onchange="() => ApplyAccountEndpoint(activeAccount)"
                                           @onkeydown="e => OnAccountEndpointKeyDown(e, activeAccount)" />

                                <p class="setting__status" data-testid="account-status" role="status">
                                    @if (AccountProblem(activeAccount) is { } problem)
                                    {
                                        <span class="setting__status--error">@problem</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@AccountSummary(activeAccount)</span>
                                    }
                                </p>

                                <p class="setting__note">
                                    Accounts are kept in <code>@GitHub.Settings.SettingsPath</code> - deliberately
                                    outside the backlog folder, so they are never synced or committed with entries.
                                    A token the GitHub CLI hands over is never written there at all.
                                </p>
                            </ChildContent>
                        </TabPanel>
                    }
                </Tabs>
            }
        </TabPanel>
    }

        <TabPanel Id="repositories"
                  Title="Repositories"
                  Element="section"
                  BaseClass="setting"
                  TestId="github-settings"
                  aria-label="Repository settings">
            <h2 class="setting__title">Repositories</h2>
            <p class="setting__body">
                Configure zero or more repositories Backlog can work with. GitHub needs an
                <code>owner/repo</code> connection; local features also
                need the clone directory on this machine.
            </p>

            @* The box carries its own border through `setting__input`, so the
               library's grow wrapper is emitted without one and auto-grow stays
               off - the rows count is what sizes this field. *@
            <TextArea Bare="true"
                      AutoGrow="false"
                      GrowCssClass=""
                      LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                      InputCssClass="@($"{SettingInputClass(_repoError)} setting__input--multiline")"
                      Label="@RepositoryInputLabel"
                      Id="github-repos"
                      data-testid="github-repos-input"
                      Rows="@RepositoryInputRows"
                      spellcheck="false"
                      autocomplete="off"
                      aria-describedby="github-repos-status"
                      Placeholder="@RepositoryInputPlaceholder"
                      Value="@_draftRepos"
                      ValueChanged="value => _draftRepos = value"
                      @onchange="ApplyRepositories" />

            <p class="setting__status" id="github-repos-status" data-testid="github-repos-status" role="status">
                @if (_repoReplacedHint is not null)
                {
                    @* Said once, on the save that did it, and beside the ordinary
                       summary rather than instead of it. Not an error — the save
                       went through — but the one edit in this box that reads like a
                       rename and is not one deserves a sentence pointing at the
                       control that is. *@
                    <span data-testid="github-repos-replaced-hint">@_repoReplacedHint </span>
                }
                @if (_repoError is not null)
                {
                    <span class="setting__status--error">@_repoError</span>
                }
                else if (GitHub.Settings.RegistryError is { } registryError)
                {
                    @* Said on load rather than only when somebody tries to write.
                       An unreadable registry composes to an empty list, and the
                       empty-list message below would read as "nobody has
                       configured one yet" - which is the opposite of the truth and
                       invites reconfiguring from scratch over a file that is
                       intact and simply unparseable. Naming the file is the
                       actionable half: it is the one thing to go and look at. *@
                    <span class="setting__status--error">@registryError</span>
                    <span>The registry is <code>@GitHub.Settings.RegistryPath</code>. Repositories stay as they are until it can be read.</span>
                }
                else if (!VisibleRepositories.Any())
                {
                    <span>Nothing configured - entries show no repository controls until one is.</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span>
                        <code>@VisibleRepositories.First().FullName</code> is configured@(VisibleRepositories.Count > 1 ? $", and {VisibleRepositories.Count - 1} more." : ".")
                        @if (AdditionalRepositoriesEnabled)
                        {
                            <span>Type <code>@("@" + VisibleRepositories.First().Alias)</code> on an entry to assign it to <code>@VisibleRepositories.First().FullName</code>.</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>The first configured repository is used for the single-repository backlog experience.</span>
                        }
                    </span>
                }
            </p>

            <div class="setting__actions">
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                           data-testid="add-repository-button"
                           OnClick="AddRepositoryDraft">
                    Add repository
                </AppButton>
            </div>
            @if (VisibleRepositories.Any())
            {
                @* One subpage per repository, same shared strip as the page tabs
                   above - only the classes differ. *@
                <Tabs Bare="true"
                      ListCssClass="repo-subpages"
                      ListTestId="repo-subpages"
                      AriaLabel="Repository pages"
                      TabCssClass="repo-subpage"
                      ActiveTabCssClass="repo-subpage repo-subpage--active"
                      ActiveId="@ActiveRepository?.Alias"
                      ActiveIdChanged="ShowRepositoryPage">
                    @foreach (var repository in VisibleRepositories)
                    {
                        var activeRepo = repository;

                        <TabPanel Id="@activeRepo.Alias"
                                  TabTestId="repo-subpage-tab"
                                  Element="article"
                                  BaseClass="repo-card"
                                  TestId="github-repo-card"
                                  aria-label="@($"{activeRepo.FullName} repository settings")">
                            <TitleContent>
                                <span>@activeRepo.FullName</span>
                            </TitleContent>
                            <ChildContent>
                        <header class="repo-card__header">
                            <div>
                                <h3 class="repo-card__title">@activeRepo.FullName</h3>
                                <p class="repo-card__meta">
                                    Area <code>@("@" + activeRepo.Alias)</code>
                                </p>
                                @if (_renameNoteAlias == activeRepo.Alias && _renameNote is not null)
                                {
                                    @* Said once, on the card it concerns, beside the
                                       name it now carries: a rename is a result to
                                       report, not an error to clear. *@
                                    <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-rename-note" role="status">@_renameNote</p>
                                }
                            </div>

                            @* Rename before Remove, in the order somebody reaching
                               for one of them would want to meet them: the one that
                               keeps everything, then the one that keeps nothing. *@
                            <div class="repo-card__actions">
                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                           data-testid="rename-repository-button"
                                           OnClick="() => BeginRename(activeRepo)">
                                    Rename
                                </AppButton>
                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                           data-testid="remove-repository-button"
                                           OnClick="() => RemoveRepository(activeRepo)">
                                    Remove repository
                                </AppButton>
                            </div>
                        </header>

                        @if (_renamingAlias == activeRepo.Alias)
                        {
                            @* A rename is asked for by name rather than read out of
                               the repositories box above, because the box cannot tell
                               a rename from a replacement — and for a line written
                               without an alias of its own, the two are the same edit.
                               Asked for here, the repository keeps its clone directory,
                               colour, account and devbook settings under the new name,
                               and every entry and inbox item filed against the old
                               name follows it. *@
                            <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-rename">
                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                           LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                           InputCssClass="@SettingInputClass(_renameError)"
                                           Label="@($"New name for {activeRepo.FullName}")"
                                           Id="@($"rename-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                           data-testid="repo-rename-input"
                                           spellcheck="false"
                                           autocomplete="off"
                                           aria-describedby="@($"rename-status-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                           Placeholder="owner/repo"
                                           Value="@_renameDraft"
                                           ValueChanged="value => _renameDraft = value"
                                           @onkeydown="e => OnRenameKeyDownAsync(e, activeRepo)" />
                                <p class="setting__status" id="@($"rename-status-{activeRepo.Alias}")" data-testid="repo-rename-status" role="status">
                                    @if (_renameError is not null)
                                    {
                                        <span class="setting__status--error">@_renameError</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>The repository keeps its settings under the new name, and every entry and inbox item filed against <code>@activeRepo.FullName</code> follows it.</span>
                                    }
                                </p>
                                <div class="setting__actions">
                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               data-testid="repo-rename-apply"
                                               OnClick="() => ApplyRenameAsync(activeRepo)">
                                        Rename repository
                                    </AppButton>
                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               data-testid="repo-rename-cancel"
                                               OnClick="CancelRename">
                                        Cancel
                                    </AppButton>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        }

                        @* Which colour this repository wears everywhere it appears —
                           the filter above the backlog, its roadmap band, its entries
                           and the sessions under them. Here rather than on any one of
                           those surfaces, because it is one fact about the repository
                           and a surface that chose its own would be a second answer to
                           the same question.

                           A radiogroup: five hues and a default, exactly one of which
                           holds at a time. Reset is a button and not a sixth swatch —
                           it is not one more colour to sit among them, it is the
                           taking back of a choice. *@
                        <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-colour">
                            <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">Colour</h4>
                            <p class="setting__note">
                                A quiet marker on this repository's filter, roadmap band and entries. Leave it on default and Backlog picks one that no other repository is using.
                            </p>

                            <div class="repo-swatches" role="radiogroup" aria-label="@($"Colour for {activeRepo.FullName}")">
                                @for (var option = 1; option <= RepositoryColours.Available; option++)
                                {
                                    var colour = option;
                                    var chosen = activeRepo.Colour == colour;

                                    <AppButton BaseClass="@($"repo-swatch repo-swatch--{colour}")"
                                               Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               CssClass="@(chosen ? "repo-swatch--chosen" : null)"
                                               TestId="@($"repo-colour-{colour}")"
                                               role="radio"
                                               aria-checked="@(chosen ? "true" : "false")"
                                               aria-label="@($"Colour {colour}")"
                                               Title="@($"Colour {colour}")"
                                               OnClick="() => ApplyRepositoryColour(activeRepo, colour)" />
                                }

                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                           Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                           TestId="repo-colour-reset"
                                           Disabled="@(activeRepo.Colour is null)"
                                           OnClick="() => ApplyRepositoryColour(activeRepo, null)">
                                    Reset to default
                                </AppButton>
                            </div>

                            <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-colour-status" role="status">
                                @RepositoryColourSummary(activeRepo)
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        @* Which of this machine's accounts calls for this repository go
                           out as. Beside the colour and for the same reason: it is one
                           fact about the repository rather than about any one surface,
                           and it is shared workspace data, so it lives here rather than
                           in the textarea's grammar - which is a thing you type, while
                           an account is a thing you pick.

                           A SelectField and not a radiogroup of buttons. A colour has to
                           be seen to be chosen; an account is a name from a list, which
                           is the shape the library already draws - and its empty option
                           carries the unbound state, so nothing has to be reset. *@
                        @if (Features.IsEnabled(TasksFeatures.GitHubIntegration))
                        {
                            <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-account">
                                <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">Account</h4>
                                <p class="setting__note">
                                    Leave it on the default and calls go out as whichever account this
                                    machine is signed in as, which is what Backlog has always done.
                                    Accounts are added on the Accounts tab.
                                </p>

                                <SelectField Form="true"
                                             Label="Worked as"
                                             Id="@($"repo-account-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                             TestId="repo-account-select"
                                             LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                             SelectCssClass="setting__input"
                                             CurrentValue="@activeRepo.Account"
                                             Options="@AccountOptions(activeRepo)"
                                             IncludeEmptyOption="true"
                                             EmptyLabel="Default (whichever account this machine is signed in as)"
                                             HelpText="@($"The identity {activeRepo.FullName}'s calls leave as.")"
                                             OnChanged="login => ApplyRepositoryAccount(activeRepo, login)" />

                                <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-account-status" role="status">
                                    @{ var binding = RepositoryBinding(activeRepo); }
                                    @if (binding.IsUnsatisfied)
                                    {
                                        <span class="setting__status--error">@BindingProblem(binding)</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@BindingSummary(binding)</span>
                                    }
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        }

                        @* Two columns: how this machine reaches the repository,
                           and which of its knowledge folders Backlog reads. *@
                        <div class="setting-columns">
                            <div>
                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                           LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                           InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                           Label="Local clone directory"
                                           Id="@($"clone-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                           data-testid="repo-clone-directory-input"
                                           spellcheck="false"
                                           autocomplete="off"
                                           Placeholder="@($"C:\\Repos\\{activeRepo.Name}")"
                                           Value="@CloneDirectoryDraft(activeRepo)"
                                           ValueChanged="value => _draftCloneDirectories[activeRepo.Alias] = value"
                                           @onchange="() => ApplyCloneDirectory(activeRepo.Alias)"
                                           @onkeydown="e => OnClonePathKeyDown(e, activeRepo)" />
                                <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-clone-status" role="status">
                                    @{ var cloneStatus = CloneStatus(activeRepo); }
                                    @if (cloneStatus.IsCloned)
                                    {
                                        <span>Local clone: <code>@cloneStatus.CloneDirectory</code></span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@cloneStatus.Summary</span>
                                    }
                                </p>
                                <div class="setting__actions">
                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               data-testid="repo-clone-button"
                                               Disabled="@(!CanClone(activeRepo))"
                                               OnClick="() => CloneRepositoryAsync(activeRepo)">
                                        @CloneButtonText(activeRepo)
                                    </AppButton>
                                </div>

                                @* Where this repository's knowledge is read from.
                                   One control for what is stored as two settings:
                                   the branch travels with the workspace, the
                                   decision to read the clone instead is this
                                   machine's, and nobody choosing between them
                                   thinks of that as two questions. *@
                                <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-devbook-source">
                                    <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">Devbook source</h4>
                                    @* Keyed for the reason the pane's copy is:
                                       loading the branch list has to rebuild the
                                       control, or the browser keeps the value of
                                       the entry that triggered the load and shows
                                       a branch nobody selected. *@
                                    <SelectField @key="@($"{activeRepo.Alias}:{DevbookSource.HasBranches(activeRepo.Alias)}")"
                                                 LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                 SelectCssClass="setting__input"
                                                 Label="Read the devbook from"
                                                 Id="@($"devbook-source-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                                 TestId="repo-devbook-source-select"
                                                 CurrentValue="@DevbookSource.CurrentValue(activeRepo.Alias)"
                                                 Options="@DevbookSource.Options(activeRepo.Alias)"
                                                 OnChanged="value => ApplyDevbookSourceAsync(activeRepo, value)" />
                                    <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-devbook-source-status" role="status">
                                        @DevbookSource.Summary(activeRepo.Alias)
                                    </p>
                                    <div class="setting__actions">
                                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                   data-testid="repo-devbook-branches-button"
                                                   Disabled="@_loadingBranches"
                                                   OnClick="() => LoadBranchesAsync(activeRepo)">
                                            @(_loadingBranches ? "Loading branches..." : "Load branches")
                                        </AppButton>
                                    </div>
                                    <Alert Message="@_branchError" TestId="repo-devbook-branches-error" />
                                </div>

                                @* The dashboard's pull-request detail is kept on
                                   this machine because a merged pull request's
                                   reviews, churn and size cannot change again.
                                   That is only true while the copy matches the
                                   repository, so there has to be a way back -
                                   and it is per repository, because a rewritten
                                   history is one repository's problem and
                                   re-reading the others would be a long fetch
                                   for nothing. Present only when the app is
                                   actually keeping one, the way the Devices
                                   panel treats its collaborators. *@
                                @if (_activityCache is not null)
                                {
                                    <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-activity-cache">
                                        <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">Dashboard activity</h4>
                                        <p class="setting__note">
                                            Merged pull requests and closed issues are kept on this machine, with each pull request's review, churn and size detail, so opening the dashboard only walks the pages that changed since and fetches the pull requests it has not seen. Nothing about a merged pull request changes, so the saved copy stays right unless <code>@activeRepo.FullName</code> had its history rewritten.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="repo-activity-cache-status" role="status">
                                            @ActivityCacheStatus(activeRepo)
                                        </p>
                                        <div class="setting__actions">
                                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                       data-testid="repo-activity-cache-forget"
                                                       OnClick="() => ForgetActivityCache(activeRepo)">
                                                Forget this repository's saved pull requests and issues
                                            </AppButton>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                }

                                @if (Features.IsEnabled(TasksFeatures.GitHubIntegration))
                                {
                                    <div class="repo-card__section" data-testid="repo-github-access">
                                        <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">GitHub access</h4>
                                        <p class="setting__note">
                                            Signing in with the GitHub CLI is preferred. This repository token is only used as a fallback for <code>@activeRepo.FullName</code> when <code>gh</code> is not signed in.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="github-connection-status" role="status">
                                            @(_connection?.Summary ?? "Checking how this machine can reach GitHub...")
                                        </p>
                                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                   Label="Personal access token"
                                                   Id="@($"github-token-{activeRepo.Alias}")"
                                                   data-testid="github-token-input"
                                                   Type="password"
                                                   spellcheck="false"
                                                   autocomplete="off"
                                                   Placeholder="@(activeRepo.Token is null ? "ghp_..." : "stored - hidden")"
                                                   Value="@RepositoryTokenDraft(activeRepo)"
                                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftTokens[activeRepo.Alias] = value"
                                                   @onchange="() => ApplyRepositoryTokenAsync(activeRepo)"
                                                   @onkeydown="e => OnRepositoryTokenKeyDownAsync(e, activeRepo)" />
                                        <div class="setting__actions">
                                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                       data-testid="github-recheck-button"
                                                       OnClick="CheckConnectionAsync">
                                                Check the connection
                                            </AppButton>
                                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                                       data-testid="github-clear-token-button"
                                                       Disabled="@(activeRepo.Token is null)"
                                                       OnClick="() => ClearRepositoryTokenAsync(activeRepo)">
                                                Forget this repository token
                                            </AppButton>
                                        </div>
                                        <p class="setting__note">
                                            Tokens are kept in <code>@GitHub.Settings.SettingsPath</code> - deliberately outside the backlog folder, so they are never synced or committed with entries.
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>

                            <div class="devbook-folders" data-testid="devbook-folder-settings">
                                <h4 class="devbook-folders__title">Devbook sections</h4>
                                <p class="setting__note">
                                    Repository knowledge folders default to their conventional paths.
                                    Clear an override to return to the default, or turn a section off for this repository.
                                    Instructions are on/off only and use Backlog's standard repository discovery.
                                </p>

                                <div class="devbook-folder-list">
                                    @foreach (var folder in activeRepo.DevbookFolders)
                                    {
                                        var devbookInputId = $"devbook-{activeRepo.Alias}-{folder.Key.TrimStart('.')}";

                                        @* Asked of the module port rather than checked here, so the row
                                           reports what a reader of this folder would actually get - and
                                           says "add a clone directory" or "not a valid path" where those
                                           are the real answer, instead of a flat "missing". Nothing to
                                           resolve for a section that is off or has no folder of its own. *@
                                        var location = folder.Enabled && folder.SupportsPathOverride
                                            ? DevbookFolders.Resolve(folder.Key, activeRepo.Alias)
                                            : null;

                                        <div class="devbook-folder" data-testid="devbook-folder-row">
                                            <Checkbox CssClass="devbook-folder__toggle"
                                                      Label="@folder.DisplayName"
                                                      Checked="@folder.Enabled"
                                                      CheckedChanged="enabled => SetDevbookFolderEnabled(activeRepo, folder, enabled)"
                                                      data-testid="devbook-folder-enabled">
                                                <code>@folder.Key</code>
                                            </Checkbox>

                                            @if (folder.SupportsPathOverride)
                                            {
                                                <TextField Bare="true"
                                                           InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                                           Id="@devbookInputId"
                                                           data-testid="devbook-folder-path-input"
                                                           spellcheck="false"
                                                           autocomplete="off"
                                                           Disabled="@(!folder.Enabled)"
                                                           Placeholder="@folder.DefaultRelativePath"
                                                           AriaLabel="@($"{activeRepo.FullName} {folder.DisplayName} folder path")"
                                                           Value="@DevbookPathDraft(activeRepo, folder)"
                                                           ValueChanged="value => _draftDevbookPaths[DevbookDraftKey(activeRepo.Alias, folder.Key)] = value"
                                                           Suffix="@DevbookFolderMarker(location)"
                                                           @onchange="() => ApplyDevbookFolderPath(activeRepo, folder)"
                                                           @onkeydown="e => OnDevbookPathKeyDown(e, activeRepo, folder)" />
                                            }

                                            <p class="devbook-folder__status"
                                               data-testid="devbook-folder-status"
                                               data-folder-state="@DevbookFolderState(location)">
                                                @if (!folder.Enabled)
                                                {
                                                    <span>Off for this repository.</span>
                                                }
                                                else if (!folder.SupportsPathOverride)
                                                {
                                                    <span>Uses standard repository instruction discovery.</span>
                                                }
                                                else
                                                {
                                                    @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(folder.Path))
                                                    {
                                                        <span>Uses <code>@folder.DefaultRelativePath</code> at the repository root.</span>
                                                    }
                                                    else
                                                    {
                                                        <span>Uses <code>@folder.EffectivePath</code>.</span>
                                                    }

                                                    @* Nothing is added when the folder is there: the marker in the
                                                       field above has already said so, and a sentence repeating it
                                                       was the redundancy. Only the absent case has something left
                                                       to say - which path was looked at, or that no clone directory
                                                       is configured yet - and the reason comes from the port rather
                                                       than being reworded here, because which of the three ways a
                                                       folder can be absent it is decides what to do about it. *@
                                                    @if (!location!.Available)
                                                    {
                                                        @* The space is written out because Razor drops whitespace-only
                                                           text between elements, and these two spans are one sentence
                                                           apiece: without it the line reads "at the repository
                                                           root.Architecture knowledge folder was not found at ...". *@
                                                        @(" ")
                                                        @* A branch being fetched for the first time is news, not a
                                                           fault: nothing here is wrong and nothing needs fixing, so it
                                                           wears the pending modifier and the row re-renders when the
                                                           folder source announces the download landed. *@
                                                        <span class="@(location.Pending ? "devbook-folder__status--pending" : "devbook-folder__status--error")">@location.Message</span>
                                                    }
                                                }
                                            </p>
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                            </ChildContent>
                        </TabPanel>
                    }
                </Tabs>
            }
        </TabPanel>

    @if (IsSettingsPageAvailable(SettingsPage.Devices))
    {
        <TabPanel Id="devices" Title="Devices" Element="section" BaseClass="setting" aria-label="Device settings">
            @* Where the cards below send their traffic. First, because when it is
               wrong nothing under it works and the only other sign is a DNS error
               naming a host called "sync". Under the AppHost the field stays blank
               and the line says so; the installed app has no AppHost and needs
               the URL from here or from the environment. *@
            @if (_syncService is not null && _syncServiceEndpoint is not null)
            {
                <section class="setting" data-testid="sync-service-settings" aria-label="Sync service">
                    <h2 class="setting__title">Sync service</h2>
                    <p class="setting__body">
                        The service this device pairs through and replicates to. Leave it
                        blank when the app is started from the Aspire AppHost, which finds
                        that run's own service by itself.
                    </p>

                    <TextField Bare="true"
                               LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                               InputCssClass="setting__input"
                               Label="Service URL"
                               Id="sync-service-url"
                               data-testid="sync-service-url-input"
                               Type="url"
                               spellcheck="false"
                               autocomplete="off"
                               Placeholder="https://backlog-sync.example.azurecontainerapps.io"
                               Value="@_draftSyncServiceUrl"
                               ValueChanged="value => _draftSyncServiceUrl = value"
                               @onchange="ApplySyncServiceUrlAsync"
                               @onkeydown="OnSyncServiceKeyDownAsync" />

                    <p class="setting__status @(_syncServiceFailed ? "setting__status--error" : null)"
                       data-testid="sync-service-status"
                       role="@(_syncServiceFailed ? "alert" : "status")">
                        @if (_syncServiceMessage is not null)
                        {
                            <span>@_syncServiceMessage</span>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span>@SyncServiceStatusLine</span>
                        }
                    </p>

                    <p class="setting__note">
                        Kept in <code>@_syncService.SettingsPath</code> - outside the backlog folder, so it is never synced or committed with entries.
                        <code>@SyncServiceEndpoint.EnvironmentVariable</code> in the environment is used when this is blank.
                    </p>
                </section>
            }

            @* A device is in one of two states and each has exactly one thing to do
               next, so the cards come in pairs: unpaired offers register and redeem,
               paired offers the code that lets the next device in. *@
            <div class="setting-columns">
                <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-status" aria-label="This device">
                    <h2 class="setting__title">This device</h2>

                    @if (_devicesBusy)
                    {
                        <Spinner Label="Talking to the sync service" TestId="devices-busy" />
                    }
                    else if (StoredDevice is { } stored)
                    {
                        @* The service has said, in as many words, that it has no
                           record of this device. Said before the identity rather
                           than after it, because everything below is describing a
                           credential that no longer opens anything. *@
                        @if (DeviceNoLongerRegistered)
                        {
                            <Alert Message="The sync service no longer recognises this device. Its credential is still on this machine, but nothing will accept it - register this device again, pair it with one that is already in, or forget the credential."
                                   TestId="devices-unregistered"
                                   Role="alert"
                                   BaseClass="setting__status"
                                   CssClass="setting__status--error" />
                        }

                        <p class="setting__body" data-testid="devices-paired">
                            @if (DeviceNoLongerRegistered)
                            {
                                <text>This device still holds a credential for <strong>@stored.DeviceName</strong>.</text>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <text>Paired as <strong>@stored.DeviceName</strong>.</text>
                            }
                        </p>
                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="devices-identity">
                            Owner <code>@stored.OwnerId</code>, device <code>@stored.DeviceId</code>.
                            @if (_deviceStatus is { } status)
                            {
                                <text>@PairedDeviceSummary(status.PairedDeviceCount)</text>
                            }
                        </p>

                        @* The one way back that needs nothing from the service.
                           A credential can go stale for reasons nobody will ever
                           be told - a service that moved, or is not coming back -
                           and deleting the file by hand was the only cure. *@
                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Danger"
                                       TestId="devices-forget"
                                       Busy="@_devicesBusy"
                                       OnClick="@(() => _forgettingDevice = true)">
                                Forget this device
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <EmptyState TestId="devices-empty"
                                    Title="This device is not paired."
                                    Description="Register it to start an owner of your own, or pair it with a device that is already in." />
                    }

                    <p class="setting__note">
                        The registration credential is kept in <code>@CredentialStorePath</code> - outside the backlog folder, so it is never synced or committed with entries.
                    </p>
                </section>

                @* Only for a device that is already one: an unpaired device has no
                   owner to replicate under, and nothing to sync. And only where a
                   host composed the loop at all - a head that registered no
                   sync-state store hides this rather than offering a button that
                   cannot work.

                   Withheld as well from a device the service has stopped
                   recognising, for the same reason as the pairing-code card
                   below it: a credential nothing will accept cannot replicate
                   anything, and the button would fail every time it was pressed.
                   The panel offers the way back instead. *@
                @if (SyncEnabled && _taskSync is not null && StoredDevice is not null && !DeviceNoLongerRegistered)
                {
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-sync" aria-label="Sync tasks">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Sync tasks</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Runs on its own every few minutes. Sends what changed on this machine and brings back what changed on the others - whole tasks, latest edit wins, so a task edited on both machines keeps one of the two versions rather than a blend of them.
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-sync-now"
                                       Busy="@_taskSync.IsSyncing"
                                       OnClick="SyncTasks">
                                Sync now
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        @* One line, and it is here so there is something to read
                           rather than because this is a sync UI. Pulled and applied
                           are separate numbers on purpose: this device's own echo
                           comes back and changes nothing, so "pulled 40, applied 0"
                           is a healthy answer. *@
                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="devices-sync-result">@TaskSyncSummaryLine</p>

                        @* Kept in its own block, below the line that says what the
                           loop has been doing, because these two are for when that
                           line stops being believable. Neither loses anything a
                           device still holds - the machine is the copy that
                           matters, and both of these are ways of saying so to a
                           replica that has drifted or been rebuilt. *@
                        <p class="setting__note">
                            Start over, if the two ever disagree:
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-sync-republish"
                                       Disabled="@_taskSync.IsSyncing"
                                       OnClick="() => _syncResetPending = SyncReset.Republish">
                                Republish everything
                            </AppButton>
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-sync-rehydrate"
                                       Disabled="@_taskSync.IsSyncing"
                                       OnClick="() => _syncResetPending = SyncReset.Rehydrate">
                                Rehydrate from scratch
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        <p class="setting__note" data-testid="devices-sync-state-path">
                            How far this device has got is kept in <code>@_taskSync.StorePath</code>.
                            @if (_logs is not null)
                            {
                                <text>A cycle that failed for a reason the sentence above does not give is written out in full under <code>@_logs.Directory</code>.</text>
                            }
                        </p>
                    </section>
                }

                @* The session loop's card, shown on the same terms as the task
                   loop's. It has less to offer - session records merge by identity
                   on the way in, so there is no rehydrate to ask for - and one thing
                   it must: a way to send every record again. A device that registered
                   again used to keep the old owner's watermark and never re-send what
                   that owner already had, and the only cure was a file to delete by
                   hand. The exchange resets itself across that line now; the button
                   is for the person whose second machine still shows nothing. *@
                @if (SyncEnabled && _sessionSync is not null && StoredDevice is not null && !DeviceNoLongerRegistered)
                {
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-session-sync" aria-label="Sync sessions">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Sync sessions</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Runs on its own every few minutes. Sends this machine's Claude and Copilot session records and brings back what the other devices reported. Only the metadata: never a prompt, a transcript, a working folder, or a session's title.
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-session-sync-now"
                                       Busy="@_sessionSync.IsSyncing"
                                       OnClick="SyncSessions">
                                Sync now
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        <p class="setting__status" data-testid="devices-session-sync-result">@SessionSyncSummaryLine</p>

                        <p class="setting__note">
                            Start over, if another device shows none of this machine's sessions:
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-session-sync-republish"
                                       Disabled="@_sessionSync.IsSyncing"
                                       OnClick="() => _syncResetPending = SyncReset.RepublishSessions">
                                Republish every session
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        <p class="setting__note" data-testid="devices-session-sync-state-path">
                            How far this device has got is kept in <code>@_sessionSync.StorePath</code>.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                }

                @if (StoredDevice is null || DeviceNoLongerRegistered)
                {
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-register" aria-label="Register this device">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Register this device</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Claims an owner of its own. Do this on the first device only - every device after it pairs instead, or it ends up with an owner nobody else can see.
                        </p>

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="Device name"
                                   Id="devices-name"
                                   TestId="devices-name"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Value="@_draftDeviceName"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftDeviceName = value" />

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary"
                                       TestId="devices-register-button"
                                       Busy="@_devicesBusy"
                                       OnClick="RegisterDeviceAsync">
                                Register
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-pair" aria-label="Pair with another device">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Pair with another device</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Type the code the other device is showing. It is single-use and expires in minutes, so it is permission to make a credential rather than a credential.
                        </p>

                        <TextField Bare="true"
                                   LabelCssClass="setting__label"
                                   InputCssClass="setting__input"
                                   Label="Pairing code"
                                   Id="devices-code-input"
                                   TestId="devices-code"
                                   spellcheck="false"
                                   autocomplete="off"
                                   Placeholder="XXXX-XXXX"
                                   Value="@_draftPairingCode"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _draftPairingCode = value" />

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary"
                                       TestId="devices-pair-button"
                                       Busy="@_devicesBusy"
                                       OnClick="PairDeviceAsync">
                                Pair
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                }
                else
                {
                    <section class="setting" data-testid="devices-generate-code" aria-label="Let another device in">
                        <h2 class="setting__title">Let another device in</h2>
                        <p class="setting__body">
                            Generate a code and read it out on the other device. Nothing travels between the two - carrying the code is what pairs them.
                        </p>

                        <div class="setting__actions">
                            <AppButton TestId="devices-generate"
                                       Busy="@_devicesBusy"
                                       OnClick="IssuePairingCodeAsync">
                                Generate a code
                            </AppButton>
                        </div>

                        @if (_issuedCode is { } issued)
                        {
                            <p class="setting__status" data-testid="devices-code-display">
                                <code>@PairingCodeFormat.Display(issued.Code)</code>
                                <CopyButton Text="@issued.Code" Label="Copy the pairing code" TestId="devices-code-copy" />
                            </p>
                            @* Refreshed by a timer rather than only on the next click:
                               the whole value of the line is that it counts down while
                               somebody is still typing the code out. *@
                            <p class="setting__note" data-testid="devices-code-expiry">@PairingCodeExpiry(issued)</p>
                        }
                    </section>
                }
            </div>

            @if (_devicesMessage is not null)
            {
                <Alert Message="@_devicesMessage"
                       TestId="devices-message"
                       Role="@(_devicesFailed ? "alert" : "status")"
                       BaseClass="setting__status"
                       CssClass="@(_devicesFailed ? "setting__status--error" : "setting__status--ok")" />
            }

            @* Escape and the backdrop both arrive on OnCancel, which is the only
               path that has to put the flag back. OpenChanged is deliberately
               unbound: it is raised before OnConfirm, so a handler that closed
               the dialog there would close it a moment before the confirm ran. *@
            <ConfirmDialog Open="@_forgettingDevice"
                           Title="Forget this device?"
                           Message="@ForgetDeviceMessage"
                           ConfirmText="Forget it"
                           Destructive="true"
                           TestId="devices-forget-dialog"
                           ConfirmTestId="devices-forget-confirm"
                           CancelTestId="devices-forget-cancel"
                           OnConfirm="ForgetDevice"
                           OnCancel="@(() => _forgettingDevice = false)" />
        </TabPanel>
    }
    </Tabs>
</div>

@* Consequential rather than destructive: neither of these loses anything, and
   both cost a long exchange and a lot of it over somebody's connection. Asked
   the way every other question with a cost on this screen is - the shared
   dialog, cancel as the default, and copy that says what will happen rather
   than what it is called. No OpenChanged binding, for the reason ToolsPane
   gives: the dialog raises it before OnConfirm, so a handler clearing the
   subject there would clear it a moment before the confirm needed it. *@
<ConfirmDialog Open="@(_syncResetPending is not null)"
               Title="@SyncResetTitle"
               Message="@SyncResetMessage"
               ConfirmText="@SyncResetConfirm"
               TestId="devices-sync-reset-dialog"
               ConfirmTestId="devices-sync-reset-confirm"
               CancelTestId="devices-sync-reset-cancel"
               OnConfirm="ConfirmSyncReset"
               OnCancel="() => _syncResetPending = null" />
@code {
    private string _draftPath = string.Empty;
    private string? _error;
    private bool _moved;
